        "thinking": "This is very revealing! The AGENTS.md has been updated by an automated linter to show that this is a fork of `paperclipai/paperclip` — the \"HenkDz/paperclip\" fork with some QoL patches. This is important context. The repo has a fork-specific section at \"## 11. Fork-Specific: HenkDz/paperclip\" which tells me a LOT.\n\nSo this is a fork, not upstream. The PRs are definitely for this fork only, as the user clarified. \n\nNow I know:\n1. `STORAGE_PROVIDERS = [\"local_disk\", \"s3\"]` — add `\"r2\"` here  \n\n\n2. `createDb` lives in `packages/db/src/client.ts` and gets exported from the index, `runningProcesses` and `runChildProcess` are in `packages/adapter-utils/src/server-utils.ts` for spawn handling, and the scheduler's setInterval logic is around line 718-783 in `server/src/index.ts`\n\nGiven the scope here, I should parallelize this work across multiple specialized backend agents tackling different PRs simultaneously since they don't all block each other — I just need to map out the dependency chain first.\n\nLooking at the dependencies, PRs #1, #2, #4, and #5 can move independently, #3 needs more codebase context, #6 waits on the interface definitions from #1, #4, and #5, #8 depends on everything up to #6, and #9 through #11 each depend on specific interfaces. So I'll spin up three agents in parallel: one handling the DB and storage work, another tackling the Scheduler and CommandExecutor interfaces, and a third starting the skeleton for the integration layer.\n\nOnce those finish, I can have more agents pick up the Durable Objects, Workflows, and adapter executors, while the HTTP handler migration—which is complex and touches many files—gets its own careful pass. The deploy button work comes last since it depends on everything else being in place.\n\nBut stepping back, delegating this much work across agents when the codebase is this large feels risky. I should probably implement the foundational pieces myself to ensure consistency, then